# AI-PLC for Codex

This repository uses the AI-PLC four-stage workflow. For Codex, invoke project skills with `$skill-name`:

1. `$01-collection` — establish the execution context and Scope.
2. `$02-inception` — decompose the Goal into an executable backlog.
3. `$03-construction` — generate task Agent definitions and execution plans.
4. `$04-operation` — execute one backlog task, verify it, update status, and propagate results.

Codex skill entrypoints are under `.agents/skills/ai-plc/`. They are thin adapters. The canonical AI-PLC runtime, Rules, DB, Wiki, and templates are installed under `.claude/`; `.claude` is a compatibility runtime here, not Codex configuration.

## Required behavior

- Before changing project state, read the selected adapter and every canonical file it requires.
- If a canonical Skill or any required Rule is missing or unreadable, report the exact path and stop without changing files.
- Follow every Mob Checkpoint and wait for human approval where required.
- Use a Codex sub-agent only when the user or an applicable instruction authorizes or requires it. Stage 4 independent review follows the canonical maker-not-checker rule.
- In Codex-facing guidance, use `$01-collection` through `$04-operation`, not Claude Code slash-command notation.
- Resolve AI-PLC DB, Wiki, Rules, and templates through the installed `.claude/` compatibility runtime.
- Never resolve canonical Claude Code native-memory references to `~/.claude`; Codex must not read or modify another tool's global native memory and records that propagation item as skipped.

## Definition of Done

A task is complete only when its declared deliverables exist, required validation passes, backlog/context status is updated when applicable, and no unresolved P0/P1/P2 verification finding remains.

## Safety

- Preserve existing user content outside AI-PLC managed files or managed marker regions.
- Do not overwrite user-data seeds such as AI-PLC SQLite databases or Wiki pages.
- Do not commit, push, tag, publish, or perform destructive Git operations without explicit user authorization.
- Never copy private absolute paths, customer data, credentials, internal Scope IDs, or secrets into public artifacts.

When both Claude Code and Codex AI-PLC sections exist, this section takes precedence only for Codex paths, launch notation, and Codex sub-agent behavior.

AI_PLC_CODEX_DIAGNOSTIC=codex-adapter-v1
